Just for reference, here is the cancellation of all the armors which provides
a cancellation > 1.  The higher the better, but if you have a cloak and armor,
nethack uses the one which provides better cancellation, and ignores the other.

Armor:
dwarvish mithril-coat     3
elven mithril-coat        3
plate mail                2
crystal plate mail        2

Cloaks:
elven cloak               3
oilskin cloak             3
cloak of protection       3
cloak of magic resistance 3
orcish cloak              2
dwarvish cloak            2
cloak of invisibility     2
cloak of displacement     2

Figuring out the overall odds of being drained are complex, but I think the
previous poster is correct: if you're wearing anything with a cancellation
of 3, the chances are 1/150 per hit.  If you only have a cancellation of
2, the chances are about 1/3 per hit, and with a cancellation of 1, it's
about 2/3 per hit, and 0 gives 3/3 per hit.

Note that all dragon scale mail provides a cancellation of 0 (even grey),
so if you're wearing GDSM, you'd better have one of the above cloaks.
(if you don't have intrinsic stealth, I'd recommend elven).
